# Domain & Data Layers

Source of truth: `iOSApp/AGENT.md` §4.

## Domain models

- Plain Swift structs/enums; `import Foundation` only
- No GRDB, Supabase, SwiftUI, or Color types

## Repository protocols (Domain)

```swift
protocol MemoryRepositoryProtocol {
    func save(_ memory: Memory) async throws
    func fetchAll(for userId: String) async throws -> [Memory]
}
```

Protocols live in `Domain/Repositories/`. Implementations live in `Data/Repositories/`.

## Use cases (Domain)

- Exactly one public `execute(...)` method
- Always pair `SomethingUseCaseProtocol` + `SomethingUseCase`
- Inject every dependency via `init`
- No UI types (`Color`, `View`, `@Published`)
- LLM calls use tiers (`.nano` / `.mini` / `.full` / `.embed`), never raw model name strings

```swift
protocol SaveMemoryUseCaseProtocol {
    func execute(text: String, sessionId: String) async throws -> String
}
```

## Data repositories

- Conform to Domain protocols
- Map GRDB/API records → domain models before returning
- Never return raw DB/API types to ViewModels or Use Cases
